    "note": "The sublattice formula of each end-member in Table 1 lists, after the two sites every end-member shares, [(CaSiO3.5)-]1 and [H2O]1, six sites with the stoichiometric coefficients 2, 2, 2, 1, 1 and 1, the last being the IW site (a vacancy or H2O). The species of each site are abbreviated here: AlH = Al0.0625O0.125H0.1875, AlNa = Al0.0625Na0.0625O0.125H0.125, CaH = Ca0.0625O0.0625H0.125, CaNa = Ca0.0625O0.0625Na0.125, SiH = Si0.0625O0.125H0.125, SiNa = Si0.0625O0.125Na0.125 (each with charge 0.125+), V = vacancy of the IW site, W = H2O on the IW site. As the paper defines it, a species on one site is distinct from the same chemistry on another. Eq. (15) gives the chemical potential of an end-member as its standard one plus RT times the sum over the six sites of the coefficient times the logarithm of the site fraction of its species; the model is ideal (no excess term) and the reciprocal terms are set to zero."
  },
