  "notes": [
    "The two sites every end-member shares, [(CaSiO3.5)-]1 and [H2O]1, carry one species each and do not enter the configurational entropy.",
    "cnash_site_mixing_terms is Appendix B transcribed on its own, independently of cnash_occupancy: each row is one term coefficient x ln(sum of the listed mole fractions) of ln(lambda_k) + ln(x_k), the logarithm of the activity of the end-member the equation is written for, in the paper's notation (5CA = 0, INFCA = 1, 5CNA = 2, INFCNA = 3, INFCN = 4, T2C* = 5, T5C* = 6, TobH* = 7). The test suite requires the two transcriptions to give the same activities.",
    "cnash_end_members gives the chemical formula Table 1 prints for each end-member; cnash_shared_sites the two sites of the sublattice formula every end-member shares. The formula of an end-member is the sum of its shared sites and of its six variable sites weighted by their coefficients, which the test suite checks against both columns.",
    "cnash_bridging_vacancies gives the ν of each end-member, which Eq. (11) turns into the minimum chain length of the gel, CL = 3/Σk(χk νk) − 1, the chains taken as not crosslinked, so a lower bound on the mean chain length, as the paper states."
  ]
}
